# BOHEMIA SIDE QUEST — PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# S02 — THE SAME CRATE TWICE
# Shape: double-agent / reputation-travels (Killian + Alpha Protocol). Faction
# wires: REDS, BLUES. Systems AS mechanic (W9): the resolution genuinely shifts
# both gangs' posture toward the player, and reputation TRAVELS — whatever you do,
# the other side hears it. The crate is salvaged batteries (the ELECTRICITY
# economy), so both blocks want it for the same real reason: to keep the lights on.
# No proper names (W8). CLOUT rides loudness of the deed, never a label: a clean
# hand-off is #notable, a quiet double-cross is #risky, keeping it for your own
# block in the open is #reckless.

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# The corpus this quest is actually built from. Every id below resolves in
# records/BOHEMIA_QUESTBOOK_LAW_INDEX.json (3,672 citable findings mined out of
# the 152 studied quests in questbook/), and gates/quest_study_gate.js verifies
# the id AND the quoted law title verbatim. A citation is a claim the machine
# can check, never a name-drop.
# @STUDY Q002.W2  THE BRANCH-ROUTER NPC
#   applied: one crate, one conversation, and every resolution routes through which side you tell it to.
# @STUDY Q001.W11  NO CLEAN WIN
#   applied: both gangs hear whatever you do; there is no route where nobody learns your name.
# @STUDY Q007.W2  EASY TO COMPLETE, HARD TO MASTER
#   applied: finishing is easy, finishing without either side hearing it is the real game, and it is self-imposed.
# @STUDY Q002.P4  W5 (fully-built villain route
#   applied: both betrayals are authored end to end; the double-cross is a designed route with its own scenes, not a punishment branch.
#
# ---- AND THE VOICE PASS (WORDS lane, 8/27/26). DEMO DAY 3. Same structure,
# ---- same branches, same effects, only the WORDS.
# ---- *** AND IT FIXED A LAW BREAK A STRANGER WOULD HAVE MET. *** THERE IS NO
# ---- MONEY (7/26, narrowed 8/15): the only legal use of the word is the dead
# ---- past, never a live transaction. This scene had FOUR: "I pay better and I
# ---- pay now", "quiet money spends the same as loud money", "(take the money,
# ---- say nothing)", and a journal line reading "Quiet money". The blues now
# ---- offer what they are actually handing over: two cases of water and a full
# ---- tank. Card: laws/BOHEMIA_VOICE_CARD_8_26_26.md
# @STUDY Q100.N2  NODE LYNETTE_MINEFIELD
#   applied: the blue boss never names the betrayal, he names the goods and lets you supply the word for what you are doing, and the offer ends on a question you have to answer to yourself.
# @STUDY Q142.W6  SILENCE EXTRACTS
#   applied: setting the crate down and saying nothing is a real branch with its own ending, and the boss reads your hands before you speak.
# @STUDY Q152.W5  THE DESPAIR SCENE CHANGES REGISTER, ONCE
#   applied: the red boss is transactional the whole scene and drops it once, for one sentence, to say what his block actually does after dark.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_same_crate   The Same Crate Twice
@ACT     1
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

@ROLE red_boss   REQ  faction=REDS   holds_block=true
@ROLE blue_boss  REQ  faction=BLUES  holds_block=true
@ROLE runner     OPT  faction_any    knows_the_load=true

@STAGE 10
  @LOG The reds want a crate of salvaged batteries on their block by dark.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20
  @LOG The blues stopped me on the road. They know what's in the crate and they're offering more.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #notable
  @LOG Delivered to the reds, closed, like I said I would. The blues heard about it.
  @DO faction REDS +10
  @DO faction_posture BLUES +1
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #risky
  @LOG Took it to the blues instead. Water and a full tank, and nobody saw. The reds get a year to work out who.
  @DO faction BLUES +12
  @DO faction_posture REDS +1
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 COMPLETE #reckless
  @LOG Kept the crate for my own block and said so to both their faces. Two enemies in one night.
  @DO faction_posture REDS +1
  @DO faction_posture BLUES +1
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 33 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Put the crate down and walked. Both sides watched me do it.

@OBJ 10  "Move the crate to the red block"   target=red_boss
@OBJ 20  "Decide who gets the batteries"      target=blue_boss

@TALK hire  speaker=red_boss  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY Batteries. Real ones, charged, not that swollen junk. My block's been dark four nights. #tired
  @SAY Get it to my door by dark and you eat for a month. Don't open it. Don't weigh it.
  @OPT "It's already moving."          [gate: none]  -> road  @DO learn carrying_batteries
  @OPT "What's really in it?"          [gate: none]  -> what
  @OPT (pick it up and go)              [gate: none]  SILENCE -> road  @DO learn carrying_batteries
  @NOVERB "Swear I will not double you"
@END

@TALK what  speaker=red_boss
  @SAY Light. That's what's in it. My people sit in the dark and listen to each other breathe.
  @SAY So stop asking and start walking.
  @OPT "Walking."                       [gate: none]  -> road  @DO learn carrying_batteries
@END

# THE INTERCEPT. The other buyer. Reputation is about to start traveling.
@TALK road  speaker=blue_boss  entry=stage>=10 and knows:carrying_batteries
  @SAY Heavy crate. Charged cells hum a little. Hear it? From here. #wary
  @SAY Those are going to a block that lets its own elders freeze so it looks tough. Bring them to mine.
  @SAY Two cases of water and a full tank, tonight, in your hands. And nobody has to know it was you. Who's going to tell them? Me?
  @OPT "A deal is a deal. This goes to the reds."   [gate: none]  -> deliver_red   @DO set_flag chose
  @OPT "Fine. Your block gets the light."           [gate: none]  TRAP -> deliver_blue  @DO set_flag chose
  @OPT "Neither. My block has elders too."          [gate: none]  -> keep_it       @DO set_flag chose
  @OPT (set the crate down between you)              [gate: none]  SILENCE -> walk_off
  @NOVERB "Ask what nobody knowing is worth to me"
@END

@TALK deliver_red  speaker=red_boss
  @SAY On time. Still closed. And I know what they put in front of you on that road. #tired
  @SAY Word travels. By Thursday the blues'll know you're somebody who finishes what he picks up.
  @OPT "Just a delivery."               [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 30
@END

@TALK deliver_blue  speaker=blue_boss
  @SAY Smart. Quiet's better. Water's by the door, take it and go home the long way. #wary
  @SAY But listen. The ones you crossed tonight are going to spend a year learning your face.
  @OPT "Let them learn it."   [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 31
  @OPT (take the water, say nothing)    [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 31
@END

@TALK keep_it  speaker=blue_boss
  @SAY You're keeping it. For your own block. And you're standing here telling us both, to our faces. #dread
  @SAY That's either the bravest thing I've seen this year or the last dumb thing you do. Two enemies in one night. Huh.
  @OPT "My block. My light."            [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 32
@END

@TALK walk_off  speaker=blue_boss
  @SAY You're going to set it down and walk. I can see it in your hands. #wary
  @OPT "Not my fight."                  [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 33
  @OPT "No. I'm choosing."             [gate: none]  -> road
@END
